# Consumer .npmrc for installing the @oopsmyops Backstage Assistant plugins
# from GitHub Packages. Copy these lines into your Backstage app's .npmrc
# (or ~/.npmrc).
#
# Provide GITHUB_TOKEN via your environment so the token never lands in a file:
#
#   Option A (developers, reuse the GitHub CLI):
#     gh auth refresh -h github.com -s read:packages   # appends the scope
#     export GITHUB_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)
#
#   Option B (PAT): create a classic token with the `read:packages` scope at
#     https://github.com/settings/tokens, then  export GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_xxx
#
# You need read access to the oopsmyops GitHub Packages registry.

@oopsmyops:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
